From: PhantoWD EX4 contributors
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: marvell: add WD My Cloud EX4 research baseline

Add a deliberately incomplete WD My Cloud EX4 device tree for compile-time
research against Linux 6.18. The raw NAND controller and SDIO remain disabled:
two published NAND unit-address names are malformed and NAND write/ECC
semantics remain unqualified, while the SDIO pin group conflicts with the
second UART used by the management controller.

The board description is derived from the GPL-2.0 device trees published by
bodhi in the Doozan EX4 thread:

  https://forum.doozan.com/file.php?2,file=7344,filename=kirkwood-wd-common.dtsi
  SHA-256: 77664ae7649f9306da8c6164a45703ecb0e6cb471759389adad30975fc8b3e45

  https://forum.doozan.com/file.php?2,file=7348,filename=kirkwood-wd-mycloud-ex4.dts
  SHA-256: df837f7a56995b579908a7dc0d038587020ab5566b8b24b66ea73f5844078af1

This patch is a non-flashable research artifact. It has not been validated on
EX4 hardware.

---
 .../bindings/arm/marvell/marvell,kirkwood.yaml     |  1 +
 arch/arm/boot/dts/marvell/Makefile                 |  3 +-
 .../dts/marvell/kirkwood-wd-mycloud-ex4.dts        | 113 +++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 116 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm/boot/dts/marvell/kirkwood-wd-mycloud-ex4.dts

